tkl-installer (0.1.2+keel5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The reboot after the install works when the live medium is gone. The
    installer asks the operator to remove the medium, and the reboot
    program is a file of that medium: its exec failed with EIO and the
    machine stayed in the live system ("OSError: [Errno 5] Input/output
    error: 'reboot'", VM 9367 on BR1, 2026-11-06). The kernel's own reboot
    (SysRq b) now takes over when the program cannot run or fails; the
    filesystems of the target are unmounted and synced before.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

tkl-installer (0.1.2+keel4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The installer shows the Keel Linux name: "Keel Linux Installer" is the
    title and the backtitle of each screen, the start screen says "Keel
    Linux Live Installer", and the unit that systemd names on the console
    and the help text of the command say "Keel Linux". Before, each screen
    said "TurnKey Installer" and the first boot that follows said "Keel
    Linux - First boot configuration" (commissioning test of the WordPress
    ISO on a Proxmox VM on BR1, 2026-11-06). The package, the command and
    the LVM volume group keep their names.
  * tests/test_branding.py holds these texts, and the build runs it.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

